runRunCmd(app directory, runtime flags) starts the coordinator with the application classpath and main class.
runBuildCmd(app directory, output path, source path, main class) builds a standalone native runtime binary.
Collect class definitions, validate names and syntax, and report foreign directories excluded from embedding.
Stage non-test runtime sources, dependency metadata, vendored dependencies and web assets in a temporary build tree.
Stage application definitions, generate their embedded filesystem binding, and compile the requested binary.
Preserve terminal scripts, stylesheets, licenses and source provenance in standalone builds.
Locate runtime sources from explicit directory, compile-time source location or current directory.
Copy operations create required directories and report file errors.
